WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.680
Did you spot the two Anzellans in the most&nbsp;
recent trailer? Have you heard that a "Back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:09.000
to the Future" star will reportedly make&nbsp;
an appearance? Here's everything you need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.588
to know about "The Mandalorian"&nbsp;
Season 3 before the big premiere.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:20.400
The wait for "The Mandalorian" Season 3 is almost&nbsp;
over. At Brazil's CCXP in December 2022, it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:25.380
announced that the third season of the Disney+&nbsp;
"Star Wars" series would be premiering on March 1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:30.840
2023. Granted, the stretch of time between&nbsp;
Season 2 and Season 3 has been pretty long,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:35.160
as the second season hit Disney+&nbsp;
all the way back in October 2020.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:40.680
Din Djarin did, of course, continue his journey&nbsp;
in a few episodes of "The Book of Boba Fett"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:45.060
alongside that titular character, but it's&nbsp;
been a while since he was front and center&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:50.820
on his own show. But now, his return is nigh.&nbsp;
Of course, if you're itching for more "Star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:55.920
Wars" to hold you over until then, there's&nbsp;
plenty of content on Disney+, from other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:01.860
Disney+ series to the actual "Star Wars" movies&nbsp;
themselves. Or it might be the perfect time to go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:06.600
back and revisit Din Djarin's adventures in&nbsp;
the first two seasons of "The Mandalorian."

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.240
There have been two trailer drops thus far,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:14.640
which have undoubtedly wetted the appetites&nbsp;
of many fans. From Djarin's homeworld of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:20.220
Mandalore to Grogu using the force to throw&nbsp;
an enemy, we're all excited for March 1st.

00:01:20.649 --> 00:01:26.580
"The Mandalorian" Season 3 will feature a major&nbsp;
change of scenery as Din Djarin travels to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:31.860
his homeworld of Mandalore, the planet of the&nbsp;
Mandalorians. Djarin hasn't been on Mandalore&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:36.600
since he was a child. There's no telling what the&nbsp;
journey will bring as we've only heard stories of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:41.340
the war that destroyed the once-great planet&nbsp;
and drove the Mandalorian across the galaxy.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:44.820
In footage screened at the&nbsp;
2022 "Star Wars" Celebration,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:49.140
Djarin says he's headed to Mandalore to&nbsp;
seek forgiveness for his transgressions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:54.540
The worst of which was him removing his&nbsp;
helmet by choice in order to rescue Grogu.

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:59.306
"Then you are a Mandalorian no more."

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:05.760
There, he'll have to bathe in a pool of water&nbsp;
in order to wash away his sins. Speaking with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:12.000
IGN in September 2022, executive producer&nbsp;
Rick Famuyiwa confirmed that Mando grappling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.680
with his Season 2 decision would be a major&nbsp;
part of the upcoming installment. He said,

00:02:29.621 --> 00:02:34.860
Of course, things will get complicated once Din&nbsp;
Djarin returns to his homeworld. As we know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:40.740
he belongs to a very specific sect of Mandalorians&nbsp;
who never remove their helmets — the Children of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:46.080
the Watch. However, that doesn't apply to most&nbsp;
other Mandalorians, something showrunner Jon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:50.940
Favreau elaborated on while talking to&nbsp;
the Dagobah Dispatch Podcast. He said,

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:09.900
It probably won't help matters that Mando&nbsp;
is in possession of the fabled Darksaber,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:14.640
a legendary blade that Mandalorian&nbsp;
leader Bo-Katan Kryze desperately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:18.540
wants to get her hands on. And of&nbsp;
course, the remnant of the Galactic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:22.860
Empire will be working in the shadows,&nbsp;
as the official plot synopsis reads,

00:03:33.744 --> 00:03:40.966
"Alright, kid. Hang on. You&nbsp;
ready for an adventure?"

00:03:40.966 --> 00:03:46.620
Never fear — Pedro Pascal is, of course,&nbsp;
returning as Din Djarin. And he won't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:51.900
be the only familiar actor coming back.&nbsp;
Giancarlo Esposito will reprise his role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:56.100
as the villainous Moff Gideon. Carl&nbsp;
Weathers is returning to play Greef&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.100 --> 00:04:00.840
Karga. Katee Sackhoff will be making&nbsp;
things interesting as Bo-Katan Kryze.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:05.520
Additionally, expect to see Amy&nbsp;
Sedaris as mechanic Peli Motto,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:10.980
Omid Abtahi as Imperial scientist Dr.&nbsp;
Pershing, and Paul Sun-Hyung Lee as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:16.080
New Republic pilot Captain Carson Teva. And&nbsp;
of course, we'll get to hear the commanding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:21.060
voice of Emily Swallow as the Armorer, the&nbsp;
leader of Din Djarin's Mandalorian tribe.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:25.980
Of course, there will be plenty of new faces&nbsp;
as well, and if you're a fan of "Back to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:31.200
Future" or "Who Framed Roger Rabbit," then you&nbsp;
have a lot to get excited about. According to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:36.300
The Hollywood Reporter, Christopher Lloyd will&nbsp;
be showing up in Season 3, reportedly as a guest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:41.700
star. It's also been said, via ComicBook.com,&nbsp;
that comedian Tim Meadows from "Saturday Night&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:47.340
Live," "The Ladies Man," and "The Goldbergs,"&nbsp;
will make an appearance. /Film has also reported&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:53.160
that Taika Waititi will be returning to the series&nbsp;
after having played the droid IG-11 in Season 1.

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:55.307
"This is acceptable."

00:04:55.320 --> 00:05:00.120
Ever since the first season, "The Mandalorian"&nbsp;
has played host to some of the most interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:05.700
directors in the business, like Taika Waititi and&nbsp;
Robert Rodriguez. And over the course of the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:10.440
several filmmakers have been invited back again&nbsp;
and again as they seem to have that special&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:15.300
something when it comes to bounty-hunting&nbsp;
action and that emotional Mando-Grogu bond.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:19.740
According to The Hollywood Reporter, Bryce&nbsp;
Dallas Howard will be directing an episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:23.280
which makes it the third she's&nbsp;
contributed to the series thus far.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:28.200
The actor/filmmaker previously helmed&nbsp;
Season 1's "Sanctuary" and Season 2's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:32.280
"The Heiress." Greef Karga himself will&nbsp;
also be stepping back behind the camera,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:38.520
as Carl Weathers will direct at least one episode.&nbsp;
Previously, he directed Season 2's "The Siege."

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:44.100
A "Mandalorian" mainstay will also be calling&nbsp;
the shots behind the camera. Rick Famuyiwa&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:48.720
will sit in the director's chair for Season&nbsp;
3, after helming Season 1's "The Child" and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:53.220
Season 2's "The Believer." Famuyiwa is&nbsp;
going to be extremely busy this season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:58.980
as he was also promoted to executive producer,&nbsp;
alongside Jon Favreau and Dave Filoni.

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:04.080
As for newcomers, Rachel Morrison has joined&nbsp;
the director's fold. Morrison has served as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:08.820
cinematographer on projects like "Fruitvale&nbsp;
Station," "Mudbound," and "Dope." She also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:13.740
became the first woman to earn an Oscar nomination&nbsp;
for best cinematography thanks to her work on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:19.320
"Black Panther." Lee Isaac Chung is also having&nbsp;
a moment. After directing the moving indie drama&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:25.440
"Minari," he was tapped not only to helm the&nbsp;
sequel to 1996's "Twister" but also at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:31.440
one episode of "The Mandalorian" Season 3. Plus,&nbsp;
Peter Ramsey — who co-directed and won an Oscar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:35.880
for "Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse"&nbsp;
— will also be directing Din Djarin on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:39.465
his journey through a galaxy a long&nbsp;
time ago, per The Hollywood Reporter.

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:43.860
There are many creative minds working&nbsp;
behind the scenes of "The Mandalorian,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:48.240
but if we had to lay credit for the show&nbsp;
at one person's feet, those shoes would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:53.880
belong to Jon Favreau. The man behind "Iron&nbsp;
Man" and "Elf" kickstarted the whole series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:58.920
and he'll remain the showrunner in Season 3. In&nbsp;
fact, he's been at work on the new scripts for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:03.780
years, with Variety reporting all the way&nbsp;
back in April 2020 that he'd been writing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:08.340
Season 3 for quite some time. And while he&nbsp;
did pen most of the episodes by himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:14.100
he did receive some help on a few from Noah&nbsp;
Kloor and "Star Wars" mastermind Dave Filoni.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:19.260
In addition to leading the show, Favreau will&nbsp;
be executive producing alongside Filoni and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:24.780
previous "Mandalorian" director Rick Famuyiwa,&nbsp;
per Collider. With this talented trio at the helm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:30.698
we expect "The Mandalorian" Season 3 to raise&nbsp;
the bar for what "Star Wars" TV shows can be.

00:07:30.698 --> 00:07:35.760
If there's one thing "Star Wars" fans love,&nbsp;
it's digging into all the fun little details.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:40.560
On that note, what other little tidbits do&nbsp;
we know about Season 3 of "The Mandalorian?"

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:45.360
Well, the Anzellans are coming back.&nbsp;
Remember Babu Frik from "The Rise of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:50.040
Skywalker?" That's an Anzellan, for those&nbsp;
not in the "Star Wars" know. Two of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:54.480
little droidsmiths pop up in the official&nbsp;
trailer, although we're unsure if either of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:58.860
them is Babu Frik or if they're voiced&nbsp;
by original actor Shirley Henderson.

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:04.560
We've also gotten glimpses of a tree filled&nbsp;
with Kowakian monkey-lizards, so prepare for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:10.020
a lot of obnoxious laughter. It also looks like&nbsp;
the B1 battle droids are back, as these rather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:15.300
useless robots are seen in the official trailer,&nbsp;
hanging out in what appears to be a robo-bar.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:20.520
We've also heard about some of the incredibly&nbsp;
cool ships that might factor into the upcoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:25.320
season. According to ComicBook.com, two new&nbsp;
LEGO sets connected to "The Mandalorian"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:31.560
Season 3 are dropping in May 2023, with&nbsp;
one set revealing a Pirate Snubfighter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:36.600
and another revealing a Mandalorian Fang&nbsp;
Fighter vs. a TIE Interceptor. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:40.020
the official trailer seems to&nbsp;
show this exact scene in action.

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:44.220
Additionally, at Brazil's Comic-Con&nbsp;
Experience in December 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:49.620
attendees received a poster displaying some&nbsp;
Season 3 concept art. According to Collider,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:53.760
the poster depicts the Mandalorian at&nbsp;
Nevarro, the desert world with a dingy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.760 --> 00:09:00.120
town run by Karga in Season 1. However, in the&nbsp;
poster, the town now looks like a lush utopia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:05.880
indicating things have changed a lot since Din&nbsp;
Djarin's been away. The poster details seem to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:10.080
have been confirmed in the official trailer,&nbsp;
where we see Karga's community thriving.

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:14.940
We also get a glimpse of what appears&nbsp;
to be the busy city planet of Coruscant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:20.400
and the official trailer also shows a group&nbsp;
of Jedi in the Jedi Temple, bracing for what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:25.560
seems to be the onslaught of Order 66. And&nbsp;
while we don't have any inside info here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:30.300
it looks like somebody with a lightsaber is trying&nbsp;
to cut their way through the Jedi Temple door,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:34.400
indicating that Anakin Skywalker&nbsp;
could possibly be making a comeback.

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:36.694
"Make things the way we want them to be!"

00:09:36.694 --> 00:09:42.900
Perhaps most interestingly, Making Star Wars — a&nbsp;
source that usually has pretty solid "Star Wars"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:48.120
scoops — has said that Snoke's Praetorian Guard&nbsp;
will be appearing in "The Mandalorian" Season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:53.220
3. The same site has also reported that&nbsp;
we might see Moff Gideon wearing a horned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:58.560
Mandalorian helmet and that Bo Katan might be&nbsp;
sporting armor made from a fallen Mythosaur.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:04.380
These details aren't confirmed, but if they pan&nbsp;
out, they will be absolutely incredible to see.

